  "worked_solution": "We need to isolate $S,$ so we will treat the other variables $P,$ $N,$ and $A$ as constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $S.$\n\nFirst, we subtract $A$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =NS+A \\\\ P-A & =NS+A-A \\\\ P-A & =NS\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $N$ to get $S$ alone:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P-A & =NS \\\\ \\frac{P-A}{N} & =\\frac{NS}{N} \\\\ \\frac{P-A}{N} & =S\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $S=\\frac{P-A}{N}.$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that $N\\ne 0.$",
